    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick, mini.diff\n\n### Description\n\nHi echasnovski! I just found out this exported function which populates quickfix list with diff patch entries for easy navigation. So, when using this, for better preview, I use mini.pick to navigate through quickfix entries with preview enabled. But the issue is that the preview does not get updated when the quickfix list is populated using `vim.fn.setqflist(MiniDiff.export('qf'))` and stays on the same file.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.11.0-dev-1388+g39781be14b\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Have mini.pick and mini.diff setup in your configuration.\r\n2. Go to a git repo with lot of file changes which are in unstaged mode so that there are many files present in quickfix list.\r\n3. Open quickfix list entries with mini.pick quickfix picker go to preview and traverse through different entries. You can see that preview does not work properly and is not updated according to the line.\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt should update according to line.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nIt is not updating according to line.",
